  "strategy": [
    "Each Computer Engineering paper has 17 questions: five 5-mark questions in Q1, then twelve 10-mark questions (two each in Q2 to Q5, four short notes in Q6).",
    "Hyperledger Fabric architecture is asked in 8 of the 9 papers and Ethereum architecture in 7. Prepare these two first and a 10-mark choice is almost always covered.",
    "Solidity is asked in 8 of 9 papers (20 questions). Inheritance programs come up 5 times and the prime number program 3 times, so one learned program each is cheap marks.",
    "Corda, Ripple or Quorum appears as a Q6 short note in 5 of 6 Computer Engineering papers. UTXO, hot vs cold wallets, double spending and RAFT are each asked 5 times.",
    "Types of blockchain, Merkle tree and types of cryptocurrencies are each asked in 6 papers, so each is a safe pick whichever marks it carries."
  ]
